  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A guest may need a cup longer than expected, and the lending record has room for an updated return time.\", \"decision\": \"How should guests extend a loan during the gathering?\", \"goal\": \"Make cup lending and return convenient while keeping the available stock and volunteer work understandable.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood café wants to lend reusable cups at community gatherings and recover them afterward. It has a modest cup stock, washable collection crates, a simple lending record, and volunteers who can share short shifts. The plan concerns a small pilot with no deposit or sales system. Different decisions address separate moments in lending, return, and review.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nGuests choose a later return time in the lending record and ask a volunteer to confirm it. Extensions begin with the guest’s expected need.\nGuests tell a volunteer how much longer they need the cup, and the volunteer records the resulting return time. A brief conversation turns the guest’s estimate into a shared commitment.\nVolunteers offer available later return times from the lending record and let guests choose one. Extensions reflect the team’s view of future cup demand."
    }
  ],
